---
import SubpageLayout from '@layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';

const _body = `
<section class="post-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="post-hero-meta">
      <a href="/blog.html" class="section-label" style="text-decoration:none">← Blog</a>
      <span class="post-date">September 16, 2026</span>
      <span class="badge">Release</span>
      <span class="badge">WASM</span>
      <span class="badge">Embedders</span>
    </div>
    <h1 class="t-h1">Traverse v0.11.0: one real runtime.wasm orchestrator</h1>
    <div class="post-byline">
      <span>By <strong>Enrico Piovesan</strong></span>
      <span>5 min read</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="container">
  <div class="post-layout">

    <article class="post-prose">

      <p><a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/v0.11.0">Traverse v0.11.0</a> is a minor lockstep crate + npm release. The throughline is simple: native hosts and the browser embedder now drive the <em>same</em> nested-wasmi capability executor inside an application-owned <code>runtime.wasm</code>.</p>

      <div class="callout">
        Short version: one real orchestrator artifact across hosts. The browser no longer reimplements WASI / <code>emit_event</code> in TypeScript. Bundles without <code>runtime/runtime.wasm</code> (+ digest) fail closed at <code>BundleEmbedder.init</code>.
      </div>

      <h2 id="why">Why this cut exists</h2>

      <p>Before this cut, native hosts could lean on a canned WAT fixture, and the browser embedder had its own interim TypeScript WASI / <code>emit_event</code> path. That was useful while we proved nesting wasmi inside WASM (Decision 87), but it meant “portable” still had two orchestrator stories. Spec <code>1402-runtime-wasm-orchestrator-convergence</code> closes that gap on <code>main</code>.</p>

      <h2 id="orchestrator">What “one orchestrator” means</h2>

      <ul>
        <li><code>crates/traverse-runtime-wasm</code> hosts the nested-wasmi executor and the audited C-ABI export boundary.</li>
        <li>Shared, engine-agnostic <code>emit_event</code> validation and placement constraints live in <code>traverse-contracts</code>, so Wasmtime (native) and nested wasmi (<code>runtime.wasm</code>) share one core.</li>
        <li><code>RuntimeWasmHost</code> loads, dispatches, and drains lifecycle/domain envelopes from <code>runtime.wasm</code>. EventBroker durability stays host-owned.</li>
        <li>Swift/wasmi, Kotlin/Chicory, and .NET/Wasmtime pass the existing bridge conformance corpus against the real artifact. The digest is published through <code>runtime/native-runtime-registry.json</code>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="browser">Browser convergence</h2>

      <p><code>traverse-embedder-web</code> <code>BundleEmbedder</code> and <code>composedWorkflow</code> load digest-verified <code>runtime/runtime.wasm</code> from the app bundle and drive the same <code>runtime-wasm-bridge/1.0.0</code> ABI as native hosts. The interim TypeScript <code>wasi.ts</code> / <code>emitEventHost.ts</code> path and per-capability Host ABI import gating are gone. Starter and fixture bundles ship the artifact + <code>.sha256</code>.</p>

      <p><strong>Breaking for web embedder callers:</strong> bundles must include <code>runtime/runtime.wasm</code> and <code>runtime/runtime.wasm.sha256</code> (<code>sha256:&lt;64 hex&gt;</code>). Copy from this repo’s <code>runtime/runtime.wasm</code>, or resolve the published native-runtime artifact digest. Pin <code>traverse-embedder-web@0.11.0</code> together with crates at <code>0.11.0</code> — versions stay lockstep (Decision 85).</p>

      <h2 id="coming-next">Coming next: portable governed model execution</h2>

      <p>Separately from this release, work is in flight toward <strong>exact-ref governed model execution</strong> for WASM model packages — Spec <code>138-governed-exact-model-execution</code> and ADR-0074 (owner-approved; landing with implementation tickets). This is platform work on the existing Spec 137 <code>model.execute</code> host-connector port, not a new public guest import.</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Exact signed model references</strong> — app manifests pin <code>exact_model_dependencies</code>; packages carry a sidecar manifest with digest, license, ABI, schemas, and resource limits. A naked URL is never identity.</li>
        <li><strong>Provider-neutral command envelopes</strong> — versioned Spec 137 <code>model.execute</code> request/response fields with opaque <code>input_ref</code> / <code>output_ref</code> handles; host <code>stage_model_input</code> / <code>read_model_output</code> for binary tensors.</li>
        <li><strong>Registry resolve + content-addressed cache</strong> — verified cache for model packages; offline execute when the package is provisioned and the manifest allows it; miss → stable <code>model_unavailable</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>First conformance: <code>wasm-cpu</code></strong> — deny-by-default FS/network for the model guest; later acceleration adapters must preserve the public envelopes.</li>
        <li><strong>Same envelopes for browser and native</strong> — placement is metadata; browser cross-target conformance follows the native path.</li>
        <li><strong>Fail-closed</strong> — verified digest/signature, unknown fields rejected, redacted traces (no tensors/secrets/credentials).</li>
      </ul>

      <p>That arc is <em>not</em> in v0.11.0. Spec 045 (candidate / LLM resolution) stays a separate track. Guest <code>model_invoke</code> remains out of scope for v1 of Spec 138.</p>

      <h2 id="shipped">What shipped where</h2>

      <p>crates.io lockstep packages at <code>0.11.0</code> (<code>traverse-contracts</code>, <code>traverse-runtime</code>, <code>traverse-embedder</code>, <code>traverse-mcp</code>, <code>traverse-cli-rs</code>, <code>traverse-expedition-wasm</code>). npm <code>traverse-embedder-web@0.11.0</code> is published and aligned. Full notes: <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/v0.11.0">GitHub Release</a> · <a href="/changelog.html">site changelog</a> · Announcement <a href="https://github.com/orgs/traverse-framework/discussions/1440">#1440</a>.</p>

    </article>

    <aside class="post-sidebar">
      <div class="sidebar-card">
        <div class="sidebar-title">In this post</div>
        <ul class="toc-list">
          <li><a href="#why">Why this cut exists</a></li>
          <li><a href="#orchestrator">One orchestrator</a></li>
          <li><a href="#browser">Browser convergence</a></li>
          <li><a href="#coming-next">Coming next</a></li>
          <li><a href="#shipped">What shipped where</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="sidebar-card">
        <div class="sidebar-title">Related</div>
        <ul class="related-list">
          <li><a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/releases/tag/v0.11.0">v0.11.0 release →</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/traverse-0-10-2-verified-registry-mcp.html">Traverse v0.10.2 →</a></li>
          <li><a href="/blog/traverse-0-10-governed-composition.html">Traverse v0.10 →</a></li>
          <li><a href="/discover.html">Try /discover →</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </aside>

  </div>
</div>
`;
---
<SubpageLayout
  title={"Traverse v0.11.0: one real runtime.wasm orchestrator — Traverse Blog"}
  description={"v0.11.0 converges native and browser embedders onto one app-owned runtime.wasm orchestrator. Breaking for web bundles that lack the digest-verified artifact. Coming next: exact-ref governed model execution."}
  canonical={"https://traverse-framework.com/blog/traverse-0-11-0-runtime-wasm-orchestrator.html"}
  crumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Blog", href: "/blog.html" }]}
>
  <style is:global slot="head">.post-hero-meta { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .post-date { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.78rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
    .post-hero h1 { max-width: 760px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .post-byline { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--fg-muted); flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .post-byline strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 500; }
    .post-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 280px; gap: 4rem; padding: 3.5rem 0 5rem; align-items: start; }
    @media (max-width: 900px) { .post-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2.5rem; } .post-sidebar { order: -1; } }
    .post-prose { max-width: 680px; font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--fg); }
    .post-prose p { margin: 0 0 1.4rem; }
    .post-prose h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem; color: var(--fg); }
    .post-prose ol, .post-prose ul { margin: 0 0 1.4rem 1.25rem; }
    .post-prose li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
    .post-prose a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--accent-dim); }
    .post-prose a:hover { text-decoration-color: var(--accent); }
    .post-prose code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85em; background: var(--bg-elevated); padding: 0.15em 0.4em; border-radius: 4px; color: var(--accent); }
    .callout { background: var(--bg-elevated); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; padding: 1rem 1.25rem; margin: 1.75rem 0; font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--fg-muted); }
    .post-sidebar { position: sticky; top: calc(var(--nav-h) + 2rem); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.5rem; }
    .sidebar-card { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.25rem; }
    .sidebar-title { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; color: var(--fg-muted); margin-bottom: 0.9rem; }
    .toc-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; }
    .toc-list a { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.83rem; color: var(--fg-muted); text-decoration: none; display: block; padding: 0.2rem 0.6rem; border-left: 2px solid transparent; transition: color 0.15s, border-color 0.15s; }
    .toc-list a:hover { color: var(--fg); border-left-color: var(--accent); }
    .related-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.6rem; }
    .related-list a { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.83rem; color: var(--fg-muted); text-decoration: none; line-height: 1.4; }
    .related-list a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
    .sidebar-cta { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--bg-elevated), var(--bg-card)); border-color: var(--accent-dim); }
    .sidebar-cta p { font-family: var(--font-body); font-size: 0.83rem; color: var(--fg-muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.55; }</style>
  <Fragment set:html={_body} />
</SubpageLayout>
